@node sotf-engine Manual
@chapter Crate @code{sotf-engine}
@cindex sotf-engine
@cindex audio engine

@code{sotf-engine} (library name @code{sotf_audio}) is the native
multi-threaded audio engine. It owns the decode / process / playback
pipeline, the plugin host wiring, the recorder and the device
abstraction.

@menu
* sotf-engine User Guide::
* sotf-engine Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node sotf-engine User Guide
@section User Guide

End users rarely touch the engine directly -- it is driven by the
desktop and TUI players. The interesting user-facing capabilities are:

@itemize @bullet
@item Multi-format playback: FLAC, MP3, AAC, WAV, AIFF, ALAC, Vorbis
  via Symphonia; optional IAMF via feature flag.
@item High-quality resampling via @code{rubato} for arbitrary device
  sample-rate conversion.
@item Live config reload: drop a new config file in place and the
  engine picks it up (SIGHUP on Unix).
@item Multi-channel recording for measurement.
@end itemize

A minimal headless invocation is the @code{sotf-server} binary; for
embedded use, see the @ref{sotf-engine Developer Guide}.

@node sotf-engine Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Four-thread pipeline

@example
Manager  ──┬──> Decoder  ──> Processing  ──> Playback (cpal)
           │
           ├──> Config watcher / signal handler
           └──> Recorder
@end example

Each stage owns a lock-free queue. The audio callback runs on the
playback thread; it must never allocate or lock.

@subheading Key types

@table @code
@item Engine
The pipeline owner. Constructed with @code{Engine::new(config)},
started with @code{start()}, stopped with @code{stop()}.
@item NodeBuffer
Single-writer / single-reader buffer used between graph nodes. Replaces
the old @code{Arc<Mutex<Vec<f32>>>}: no locks, no clones, slice reads.
Note: @code{clear()} only resets @code{actual_len}; it does not zero
memory. @code{read()} returns the full buffer when
@code{actual_len == 0}.
@item AudioFrame
Owned @code{Vec<f32>} of interleaved samples for one quantum.
@item DawHost
Wraps @code{Arc<Mutex<Box<dyn Plugin>>>} per node; the mutex is only
ever taken outside the audio path.
@item ProcessBuffers
Extracted buffer struct that lets @code{process()} hold a mutable
borrow on its buffers and an immutable borrow on the graph topology
via @code{Option::take()} put-back.
@end table

@subheading Real-time discipline (mandatory)

@itemize @bullet
@item No allocations in @code{process()}; pre-allocate in
  @code{build()}.
@item No locks per frame; cache per-frame predicates (e.g.@:
  @code{has_variable_frame_plugin}) at build time.
@item STFT plugins return @code{context.num_frames}, not the actual
  draining count, so the ring buffer stays aligned.
@item Output clipping (@code{sample.clamp(-1.0, 1.0)}) belongs in the
  cpal callback, not inside plugins.
@item Debug builds on macOS must keep @code{opt-level = 0}; aggressive
  optimisation breaks cpal/CoreAudio device enumeration.
@end itemize

@subheading Layout

@example
crates/sotf-engine/
  src/
    engine/                pipeline + threads
    decoder/               symphonia integration, sample-rate hop
    output/                cpal device, callback
    recorder/              multi-channel capture
    config/                schema + file watcher
    analysis/              spectrum / loudness taps
@end example

@subheading Build flags

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{--no-default-features} when @code{hdf5-metno-sys} is in
  scope.
@item @code{iamf} feature enables IAMF support.
@item @code{hal}, @code{onnx}, @code{gpu-2d}, @code{gpu-3d} enable
  optional integrations.
@end itemize

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p sotf-engine --no-default-features
@end example
